Molecular contamination connects the air to the process surface (@cm-chemical-air: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Contamination-Control-Engineering-NASA.lingua#r_2XKKPYTW2DPQPQZ8VPV23BJ8A5", #source "../sources/Cleaning-and-Surface-Properties-Taborelli.lingua#r_1RDARBEFXDAW9Y2DNTJ2QBEP2E", #clean-manufacturing "Preserve-the-cleaned-state-through-handling-packaging-and-time.lingua#r_5M8MZN0TGR8FB2VBGM1TR8VA0P") { r_1ZD42S8CD5QGASSRGY76RHZP4G
**Read:** [Contamination control engineering — Tribble and colleagues, NASA CR 4740](../sources/Contamination-Control-Engineering-NASA.lingua#r_2XKKPYTW2DPQPQZ8VPV23BJ8A5), molecular-contamination transport and functional effects; [Cleaning and surface properties — Mauro Taborelli](../sources/Cleaning-and-Surface-Properties-Taborelli.lingua#r_1RDARBEFXDAW9Y2DNTJ2QBEP2E), air exposure and surface changes.

Gases and vapors can adsorb, condense, react or enter a material even when airborne particle counts are low. Identify the chemical species, source, exposure time, surface temperature and intended function. A particle filter's capture rating does not establish removal of a molecular species.

Sorbents or reactive media need their own capacity, transport and service-state account. With equal inlet and outlet volumetric flows Q, the net amount entering the control volume is ∫Q(cin−cout)dt on a consistent concentration basis. Separate changes in gas inventory, uptake into media and conversion into other species before interpreting this as captured inventory. Breakthrough depends on more than the nominal mass of media.

**Work:** Compare particle and molecular sampling for one sensitive process. Draw generation, transport, uptake and release pathways, including packaging and nearby materials. Specify an observation that distinguishes a continuously supplied vapor from release of an earlier surface reservoir. Connect later facility filtration decisions to this species-specific evidence.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
